TIP:  The lines in the verse has a complementary chord "twinkle" (e.g. "... (D) hair (G) (D)" ).  But the second lines have a sustain on the preceding chord, a dwell, and then the next chord to lead into the next line (e.g. "... (G) fall (G)(Em)".


